WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.060
The Night Troops moved
their headquarters to Karasumori.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.360
Yoshimori doesn't know how to
react to them moving in.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.160
They all place
their trust in Masamori,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.540
so they look at Yoshimori,
the Legitimate Heir,

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.510
with cold stares.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:20.780
The dangerous forest invites me
It's showtime again tonight

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.650
(Ayakashi NIGHT)

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.860
Everyone's rampaging
with all their strength

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.760
(Fighting late into the night)

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.190
Drive away all hesitation

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:37.600
Wanna take them on? Yeah

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.140
I will protect you
(No matter what)

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.470
I will protect you, that's all
(that's all I want)

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:50.140
Goodbye to the days
when all I'd do was cry

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.640
Sha la la la la...

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:01.060
I hold words in my heart
that I'd like to say

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.020
(Secret romance)

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:08.230
Standing in front of me is someone
I don't want to lose

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.990
(A strange distance)

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:16.840
I can't stand watching
people get hurt anymore

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.910
Yeah

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.380
I wanna be your knight
(I wanna be strong)

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.980
I wanna be your light
(More than I am now)

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.320
Someday I'll share with you
my 100% smile

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.610
It's far from
the Black Pampas Grass

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.120
so it might take a while
to open the passage.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.960
But I won't have to worry about
being detected here.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.260
I can focus on my technique.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.890
Whether I succeed or not...
depends on my spiritual power.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.880
How about here? You wanted
somewhere deserted, right?

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.130
So what do you want?

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.900
Say, is this where
you train Yoshimori-kun?

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.900
It's simple.
Let's play a little game.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.710
We have nothing to do
until nighttime, anyway.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:10.210
Oh, we should
introduce ourselves first.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.460
I'm Akitsu Shu.
I'm a year older than you.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.620
Nice to meet you.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.990
And over there is Yaegashi Dai.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.530
The one in the middle is...

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:21.720
Kagemiya Sen.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.300
Sen-chan is the same age as you.
Dai is one year younger.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:31.930
Sen-chan and I are part Ayakashi,
and Dai is...

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.040
All right, let's start!

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:38.280
Sen-chan!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.940
Let's go! Shu! Dai!

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.580
Hey, wait!

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.180
Wait! Three against one?!

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.820
A little handicap is okay, right?

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:51.720
Come on. Show me what
a Legitimate Heir is made of.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.260
What are you doing?
Try and catch us!

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:02.960
Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:06.530
What's going on?

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.070
Damn! They're fast!

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:14.270
All right,
I'm going to start with him!

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.540
Ketsu!

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.210
He disappeared?!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.640
Clones?!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.520
Ketsu!

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.260
The attack is only coming
from one direction.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.770
That means he's where
the attack is coming from.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:46.800
There he is!

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:50.740
Dai!

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.640
Kai! Ketsu!

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:56.520
Ketsu!

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.060
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:01.390
Ketsu!

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.360
Ketsu!

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.560
I tore my coat again!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.940
Wings? What is that?

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.380
I got your head.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:26.080
What was that?!
I didn't sense him at all!

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.780
So that's it.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.950
I expected more
from the Legitimate Heir.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:38.330
This sucks. I came
all the way here for nothing.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.170
That's...

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.040
What... are you?

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.680
Why are you even here?
Did you come here to play around?

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:06.530
What the-? He suddenly changed.
But this aura...

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.500
One of your friends is dead.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:14.830
Do you know how dangerous
the Kokuboro is?

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:19.270
I-I'm sorry, Yoshimori-kun.
We didn't mean to be disrespectful.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:24.740
Um, we're with the Battle Squad,
but we're just backup.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.810
So maybe we didn't take it
too seriously... I'm sorry.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.910
Why would I take it seriously?
This is stupid.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:33.140
Sen-chan!

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:34.510
Stupid?

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.520
Yeah, stupid.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:41.260
Even Gen lost to them.
Do you think we'd stand a chance?

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.960
He was on a totally
different level in battle.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.190
He was always on the front lines.

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:54.670
We're about the same age,
but we always watched from behind.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.010
We couldn't do anything.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.410
What about you?

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.750
When he charged at the enemy...

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:09.720
you probably couldn't do anything
and just watched from behind, right?

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:14.360
Isn't that why Gen died
and you're still alive?

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:16.550
Am I right?

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:17.850
Sen-chan!

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.460
I'm sorry!
We'll get going right away!

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.320
I'm sorry...

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:32.700
I'll avenge him...
by defeating Kaguro.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:35.810
Kaguro?

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:39.750
I'll crush the Kokuboro.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.660
Looks like you got better,
Toshimori.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.190
Yeah, kinda!

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:03.930
All right.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:09.740
Check!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.150
I lose.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.080
I finally beat you for
the first time, Masa!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.450
Yeah, I completely lost.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.790
By the way, should you be
playing right now?

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.000
Do you want to study instead?
I can help with your homework.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.970
I'm an elementary school student.
I can do my own homework.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:35.470
I see.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.910
Instead of me, maybe you should
look after Yoshi instead.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.940
Yoshimori? Why?

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:45.490
Yoshi doesn't spend
much time at home lately.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.910
I think he's training
alone in secret.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.590
Hmm, alone, huh?

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.220
Ketsu!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.100
Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.590
Ketsu! Ketsu! Ketsu!

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:01.060
Ketsu!

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:16.780
I'm quicker, but still not
fast enough to fight Kaguro.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.350
Besides, normal Kekkai
won't work against him.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.130
Ouch!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.190
You!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:34.630
Hey!

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:42.900
Huh?

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.940
So what did you want to talk about?

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.180
You're gonna lecture me again?

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.050
The Night Troops will participate
in the next battle.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.380
I can't let you go off on your own.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:58.720
You will follow my orders.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:02.050
I know.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:04.660
What? You seem
unusually obedient today.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:09.360
No reason. I'm just tired of
worrying about every little thing.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:14.140
Anyway, I'll listen to you.
Only this time!

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:15.770
But...

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:16.900
But?

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.940
Kaguro is mine.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:23.940
Is that the one that killed Gen?

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.710
I have to defeat him
with my own hands.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.380
Do you think you can win?

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.630
I-I don't know.
But if I use that...

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:34.520
That?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.960
Something weird
happened the other day.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.660
It's a bit different
from the Kekkai...

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.870
How did it feel?

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:52.640
I don't really remember,
but I remember being ticked off.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:57.110
That? He learned it by instinct?!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.860
I think that'll work
against Kaguro.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:01.980
Let me make myself clear,
Yoshimori.

00:11:02.990 --> 00:11:04.820
He's not the only enemy we have.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:08.620
Don't forget that we
must protect Karasumori.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.050
Do you understand?

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:22.870
You called for me?

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.350
Sakon, I assume you are
ready for the upcoming battle.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:33.340
Byaku-sama! That means-

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:41.490
Thank you very much!
I will seize Karasumori!

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:43.930
I am counting on you.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:45.820
Please leave it to me.

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.700
Are you dissatisfied, Shion?

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:58.740
It's not that.
You could say I have my doubts.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:03.210
You don't seem to trust Sakon,

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.720
so why do you let him
go to Karasumori?

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:09.850
It's so your Task Force Two
will have their hands free.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:12.390
So we're going to be thrown aside?

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:18.090
Our true aim this time is not
to take over Karasumori.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:20.400
Oh? I didn't know that.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.540
If Sakon can take over Karasumori,
that is fine as well.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:28.340
But I'm going to have you
do a separate job.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:33.540
Sounds like fun.
So what's that job?

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:39.710
The time has come?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.720
Yes, the Kokuboro are on the move.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.980
It looks like they
will attack soon.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:49.160
All right.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.920
I'm off!

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:54.490
Yoshimori.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.300
The Kokuboro are
making their move.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:06.700
Really?

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:09.210
My big brother says
it could be tonight.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:10.580
Oh...

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.080
Is Grandma Toki back yet?

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.020
Hey, Tokine?

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:18.020
Oh, sorry. What did you say?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.090
I said, is Grandma Toki back yet?

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:23.300
Not yet.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:24.290
I see.

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:30.760
Grandpa Shige said he'll protect
the Yukimura household,

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:31.860
so don't worry.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.700
Y-Yeah.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.870
Masamori-san is with us this time.
The Night Troops, too.

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.450
It's reassuring, but...

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:46.510
The final battle is coming.
I can finally avenge Shishio.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:49.440
Can we...

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.690
Can we really protect Karasumori?

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.160
Good morning, Tokine.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.190
Oh, good morning.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.290
Good morning.

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:02.360
Good morning.

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:09.500
Just another day,
it never changes does it?

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.750
You never change, do you?

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:20.920
Sensei! Sumimura-kun has
a reason why he's asleep!

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:22.690
Oh? And that is?

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:28.120
The reason is, um...
Because he's sleepy!

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.130
He's never sleepy
during times like this.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:38.400
Yeah. He's super awake.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.260
I've waited for this day!

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:42.230
Me, too! Sumimura!

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:43.510
Let's go!

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:44.500
Bring it!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:45.970
- Rock paper scissors!
- Rock paper scissors!

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.040
- Rock paper scissors!
- Rock paper scissors!

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.380
- Rock paper scissors!
- Rock paper scissors!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.840
All right!

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.710
I don't get guys.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.050
Their meaningless
passion for things...

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:57.960
Damn it!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:01.620
The 8th Coffee Milk Battle
has Yoshimori as the loser.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.300
Don't feel down.
According to my data,

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.700
they'll have your
favorite coffee milk

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.330
for lunch next week, too.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:13.470
What?! All right! I'm going to
have limousine next week!

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:14.980
Limousine?

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.000
He probably means "revenge."

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:20.080
What's wrong, Tokine?
You're not eating.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:23.880
Oh, I just don't have
an appetite today.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.850
Are you feeling sick?
Are you okay?

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.420
I'm fine.
So, what were we talking about?

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.460
I was saying, we were talking about
going to see a movie tomorrow.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:36.430
Flat Kidd's new movie
is coming out.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:39.770
Sorry, I can't go tomorrow.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:41.960
What about the day after tomorrow?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.830
I don't know...

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:47.670
Oh my, you shouldn't
force her to go out.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:52.950
Yukimura-san is too busy studying
to go see a movie.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:54.470
Poor thing.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.380
What's her problem?! You have to
say something to her, Tokine!

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:02.250
It's okay. I don't care.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:06.390
Oh, come on!
You're too nice, Tokine.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:10.830
I'm sorry. I'm just too busy
to go see a movie now.

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:12.830
Don't worry about it.
We'll go another time.

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.400
We'll go when you have time. Okay?

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:17.130
Sure.

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:20.710
Oh, by the way, there's this
TV show starting next month.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:22.910
It has members from that band
that performed live...

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.900
Tomorrow comes so naturally for
everyone else and they don't doubt it...

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.370
But it seems so far away to me...

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:34.290
What? You already finished it?

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:36.350
Thank you very much.

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:39.220
That was fast. It was in
the original language, too.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.550
It's not that.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.490
You can hold on to it longer,
you know.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:47.590
But it'd be bad if
I couldn't return it.

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:48.390
Huh?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.300
Oh, I just don't want to
forget about it.

00:16:58.650 --> 00:16:59.770
- And then...
- Yeah?

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:02.440
After that... you're not
going to believe this but...

00:17:23.840 --> 00:17:25.000
Yoshimori.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:29.940
It's rare of you to strike up
a conversation with me.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:33.610
I'm just wondering if these
peaceful days will continue tomorrow.

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:37.210
Huh? Of course it will.
What are you talking about?

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:41.250
But if the Kokuboro
take over Karasumori...

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:44.920
You don't know what they'll do
to this school.

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:49.590
That's not going to happen.
I won't let them.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:53.290
I'll swear on
my favorite coffee milk!

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.330
You never change.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.470
But...

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:01.170
I guess that made me
feel a little better.

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:08.620
Masamori.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:09.270
Yes.

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:13.420
Tokiko is gone,
so I cannot leave this place.

00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:16.680
You will have to protect Karasumori
with Yoshimori.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:17.750
Grandfather...

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:22.630
I still haven't accepted
the way you live your life.

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:24.700
But I won't stop you.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:27.630
If you must do it your way,
be sure to do it thoroughly!

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:32.300
I entrust Karasumori... to you.

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:34.770
Yes.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:46.420
I've gotten used to it...

00:18:46.420 --> 00:18:50.480
But it's still strange having
so many people here at night.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:55.120
Doesn't help the mood for
a midnight date with honey.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.420
Just kidding.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.600
Yoshimori, what's wrong?

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.270
You're so gloomy!

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:06.830
I wonder if he'll come...

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:08.000
What?

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:15.070
Yes?

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:17.080
Understood.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.480
Hatori, go gather everyone.

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:21.360
Yes, sir.

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.010
Hurry up.

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:24.220
Father! Father!

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.550
I just got a call from Masamori.

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:30.460
Father...

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:31.960
I know.

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:40.530
It's time for the final battle!

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:44.370
Prepare yourselves
and get in position!

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.350
There is no need to hesitate.
Don't hold back!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.310
But only under one condition!

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:54.210
There will be no casualties
on our side!

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:57.550
That's all!

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:09.360
It's finally time.

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.060
All right.

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.200
Yoshimori.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.570
Don't over think things.

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:18.140
Fight as if your life
depended on it.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.310
But... don't die.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:32.090
The enemy is coming as predicted.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.290
The problem is in
how to finish them off.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.230
If we end up having to pursue them,

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:40.790
we won't be able to follow
if they escape to the Other World.

00:20:41.240 --> 00:20:43.570
Chief. We're ready for battle.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:45.610
If that were to happen,

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:48.800
we have to rely on the passage
Grandma Tokiko is creating.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:51.640
Well, only if she's done.

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:53.600
What are you plotting?

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:55.810
Hatori.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:56.680
Yes.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:01.890
We'll make them regret that
they ever challenged us!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.860
Raizo, don't go overboard.

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.300
It's time.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:15.470
You're up first, Yaichi, Tsukinojo.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:20.030
Big Sister... do we only beat them
to within an inch of their life?

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.870
No. Go all out.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.850
You mean no restrictions?

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:31.280
I just wanted Gen to be happy.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.450
I won't forgive them!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.300
Hey, everyone! They're here!

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.820
Judging from their
speed and distance,

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.170
they'll be here in six minutes!

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:55.270
I wonder if they'll
come here again.

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:58.970
Grandpa, that black thing is
over by the school, right?

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:16.060
Humans, now you shall see
the might of the Kokuboro!

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:23.760
They're here!

00:22:46.030 --> 00:22:51.560
10 minute break,
I wanna do so much

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:59.460
Class is over, but someone
in the front asks a question

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:02.000
"What nerve"

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:05.380
I'm at ease as long as
I have a mirror

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:09.110
"Make up's on right,
my eyes look all right"

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:15.490
See, if you look behind you,
there's a girl who curled her hair

00:23:15.820 --> 00:23:20.520
I hate studying,
I like P.E. okay

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:22.460
Basketball, volleyball,
and tennis, what?

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:27.730
You're not gonna make me
run long distance today, teacher!

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:31.260
My face will get oily,
and I hate being sore

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:35.370
I'm that kind of
a beautiful high school girl

00:23:49.860 --> 00:24:00.200
10 minute break, I'll get busy
drawing a map of the future
